      {
        "url": "/journal/2025/05/03/seed-exchange/",
        "file": "journal/2025/05/03/seed-exchange/index.html",
        "title": "Seeds for the next season | Harbour Notes",
        "description": "Neighbours share seeds and the stories behind them.",
        "canonical": "https://reference.example/journal/2025/05/03/seed-exchange/",
        "visibleText": "Skip to content Harbour Notes From the east quay Journal Guides From the journal Seeds for the next season Neighbours share seeds and the stories behind them. Jon Bell · 2025-05-03 The shared garden. Original fixture illustration, CC0. On 3 May 2025, neighbours brought 18 packets of seeds to the shared garden. Each packet carried the variety, harvest year, and a short note from its grower. What to bring next time Dry seeds in a labelled paper envelope. The year you collected them. A note about the conditions they grew in. Keep a small reserve for gaps in the beds. Our seed calculator includes a 20% reserve. Harbour Notes is a fictional publication used as a Reference Site. No Client material is included.",
        "publication": {
          "id": "ref-article-002",
          "url": "/journal/2025/05/03/seed-exchange/",
          "title": "Seeds for the next season",
          "description": "Neighbours share seeds and the stories behind them.",
